{"query_id": "dp-long-chronicle", "tags": ["long-document"], "dimensions": ["long-document"], "answer": "According to the Mill Lane chronicle, Greassby Mill has the following recorded history:\n\n*   In 1860-02-24, \"Greassby Mill was sold by the estate to the miller's family, and the deed was witnessed at the inn.\" [6]\n*   Later, \"The wheel at Greassby Mill turned again for the first time since the flood, watched by most of the street.\" [3]\n*   The parish subsequently \"raised £4,525.32 by subscription to repair the roof of Greassby Mill after the gale.\" [7]\n*   At one point, \"Greassby Mill stood idle for 44 weeks while the millstones were re-dressed by a man brought in from the next county.\" [5]\n*   Regarding water flow, \"After the weir upstream was lowered, the leat at Greassby Mill carried only 17.5 per cent of its old flow.\" [4]\n*   Eventually, \"The last miller at Greassby Mill retired, and the building was let as a store.\" [2]", "answer_sha256": "0f9328d1d281f83f8f12fcd34fef3d4ce0fd263c48f89d694e09ba8eb83aaf0a", "ranked_ids": ["chronicle-long"], "citation_map": {"1": "chronicle-long", "10": "chronicle-long", "11": "chronicle-long", "12": "chronicle-long", "13": "chronicle-long", "14": "chronicle-long", "15": "chronicle-long", "16": "chronicle-long", "17": "chronicle-long", "18": "chronicle-long", "19": "chronicle-long", "2": "chronicle-long", "20": "chronicle-long", "21": "chronicle-long", "22": "chronicle-long", "23": "chronicle-long", "24": "chronicle-long", "25": "chronicle-long", "3": "chronicle-long", "4": "chronicle-long", "5": "chronicle-long", "6": "chronicle-long", "7": "chronicle-long", "8": "chronicle-long", "9": "chronicle-long"}, "cited_ids": [6, 3, 7, 5, 4, 2], "cited_document_ids": ["chronicle-long"], "invalid_citations": [], "abstained": false, "expected_abstain": false, "mechanical_checks_passed": false, "answer_correct": null, "review_status": "unreviewed", "latency_ms": 225661, "model": "Qwen3.5-9B-Q4_K_M.gguf", "error": null,